# These are copies of files that run on a Linux server. A Windows checkout must
# not rewrite them to CRLF: a shell script with CRLF line endings fails with
# "bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M", and an .env-style file parses a trailing \r
# into the value. This estate has already lost time to exactly that.
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.conf          text eol=lf
